				<h1 id="versionHeadLine" class="headline">

2026 Elections		</h1>
	
		<div id="cc5f8c90dc-b4cb-431b-90ee-10648f8df655" data-containerid="5f8c90dc-b4cb-431b-90ee-10648f8df655" class="pageContent cpGrid cpGrid24"  data-contentcontainerbreakpoint="30" >
			

		<div class="row outer wide"><!--
--><div class="outer col col24 first last" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="f886c989-719e-4677-a870-51558a4bf04d">				
	<div class="row nest first last wide">
	
	<div class="inner col col24 first last id33f1be2e-ea0a-4e2d-8756-ed2fa3c7024d" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="33f1be2e-ea0a-4e2d-8756-ed2fa3c7024d">	
<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditorc90f896c-d4cd-4d7b-912f-758cc79a0eff" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <h2 class="subhead1">November 3, 2026 General Municipal Election</h2><p>The Town of Woodside holds by-district elections for its five Town Council seats in November of even numbered years. Councilmembers serve staggering four-year terms. The General Municipal Election on November 3, 2026 is being held for two Town Council seats for full four-year terms ending 2030 in the following Districts:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>District 2</li><li>District 3</li></ul><h2 class="subhead1">Town Council Candidates</h2><p>For information on Town Council candidates or becoming a candidate, please see: <a href="https://www.woodsideca.gov/453/november-5-2024-election--town-council-candidates">November 3, 2026 Election - Town Council Candidates</a>.</p><h2 class="subhead1">Campaign Disclosure Forms</h2><p>Please see: <a href="/246/Statement-ofEconomic-Interests-Officeho" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Statement of Economic Interests &amp; Officeholder &amp; Candidate Campaign Form Information</a>.</p><h2 id="isPasted">Additional Resources</h2><h3>Register to Vote</h3><p>If you have moved, changed your name, or want to update your political party, you will need to re-register to vote. Visit the San Mateo County Elections Office <a href="https://smcacre.gov/elections/voter-registration" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Voter Registration website</a> for more information.&nbsp;</p><h3><a href="https://www.fppc.ca.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Fair Political Practices Commission</a></h3><h3><a href="https://lwvc.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">League of Women Voters</a></h3><h3><a href="https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/codesTOCSelected.xhtml?tocCode=ELEC&tocTitle=+Elections+Code+-+ELEC" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">California Election Code</a></h3><h3 class="subhead2" aria-level="2" role="heading"><a href="https://smcacre.gov/elections" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message"><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>San Mateo County Elections</strong></span></a></h3>
    </div>

<script type="text/javascript">
	$(document).ready(function (e) {		
	    renderSlideshowIfApplicable($('#divEditor' + 'c90f896c-d4cd-4d7b-912f-758cc79a0eff'));
	});
</script>
</div>

